From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:25:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Keyguard: open the bouncer with OK from a hardware keypad

On a keypad phone without a touchscreen the lock screen shows the clock
and nothing reacts to OK; the bouncer can only be reached with MENU.
OK (DPAD_CENTER) that no view on the lock screen handled now does what
MENU does: it shows the bouncer, or dismisses an insecure keyguard.

Like MENU it depends on config_disableMenuKeyInLockScreen, and it acts
only in the KEYGUARD state, so the notification shade and the bouncer
itself keep their own OK handling.
---
 .../systemui/statusbar/phone/StatusBarWindowView.java     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/StatusBarWindowView.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/StatusBarWindowView.java
index 5ebe691808d..d0444e807af 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/StatusBarWindowView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/StatusBarWindowView.java
@@ -261,6 +261,14 @@ public class StatusBarWindowView extends FrameLayout implements TunerService.Tun
                     return mService.onSpacePressed();
                 }
                 break;
+            case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_DPAD_CENTER:
+                // Without a touchscreen OK on the lock screen opens the bouncer, as MENU does.
+                if (!down && mService.getBarState() == StatusBarState.KEYGUARD
+                        && getResources().getConfiguration().touchscreen
+                                == Configuration.TOUCHSCREEN_NOTOUCH) {
+                    return mService.onMenuPressed();
+                }
+                break;
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_VOLUME_DOWN:
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_VOLUME_UP:
                 if (mService.isDozing()) {
